  "description": "Resource scheduling backend, independent of existing compute limit mutation and application runtime lifecycle. All effects retain normal Invocation identity, observational reconciliation, current owner permission and typed output custody. Neither submission acknowledgment nor scheduler completion proves Fishhat workload success. Queued workers remain inert until independently current owner resource and runtime launch guards permit the exact execution. Control work is admitted from a finite protected budget rather than recursively through this workload queue."
